      "writtenOn": "2021-01-29T23:54:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this one doesn\u0027t fit the pattern of not explicitly naming the\nKSI/KSO pins in gpio.inc, so it doesn\u0027t lend itself well to\nauto generation.\n\nthe reason we get away with not explicitly defining\nEC_KSO* and EC_KSI* in gpio.inc is because the keyboard driver\n(at least for NPCX) uses these pins without using assigned\nnames. GPIO_KBD_KSO2 (a.k.a. EC_KSO_02_INV) is the exception - it\nit is referenced explicitly.",
      "parentUuid": "f470de2e_36bc5579",
      "revId": "8712cac7dd075fed557890ecbf00875b7b5d6de3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
